{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:727bc28a41f6124c","name":"Alpha-Class Xg-1 Star Wing (CL 10)","source":{"id":"source:reference-727bc28a41f6124c","title":"Alpha-Class Xg-1 Star Wing (CL 10)","revision":24805,"timestamp":"2024-11-06T20:44:48Z","sha256":"d6fe4afa1e5f915ff0c84396c5fa70e7dbf89812eea4d489f7c34d01e2c86428","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=24805","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Alpha-Class%20Xg-1%20Star%20Wing%20%28CL%2010%29&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-727bc28a41f6124c","blocks":[{"tag":"h4","children":["Description"]},"\n",{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Web Enhancements"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Web_Enhancements"}," (",{"tag":"a","children":["Message to Spacers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Message_to_Spacers"},")"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Galactic Empire"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Galactic_Empire","referenceId":"reference:f9c9a48674cc3415"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The ",{"tag":"i","children":["Alpha"]},"-Class Xg-1 is a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighter"}," in use by ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Galactic Empire"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Galactic_Empire","referenceId":"reference:f9c9a48674cc3415"}," throughout its fleet. More commonly known as an Assault Gunboat, the \"Star Wing\" represents the Empire's first attempt at implementing a space superiority fighter in its defense force.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Wider than it is long, the Xg-1 is modeled very similarly to the well-known ",{"tag":"a","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Lambda"]},"-Class Shuttle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lambda-Class_Shuttle","referenceId":"reference:09ed6c8fc42f5b4e"}," used throughout the Empire. Its wing design also has the set dorsal fin and two primary lateral wings that fold up while in landing configuration, but the ",{"tag":"i","children":["Alpha"]},"-Class also has two additional smaller wings positioned about halfway between the dorsal fin and the primary wings that act as stabilizer fins to improve the ship's maneuverability over its shuttle counterpart. In fact, the fighter earned its nickname \"Star Wing\" from the five-point silhouette it creates when in flight mode and all five wings are extended.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Unlike the ",{"tag":"a","children":["TIE Fighters"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/TIE_Fighters"}," in common use in the Empire's navy, the ",{"tag":"i","children":["Alpha"]},"-Class gunboat has a shielding system installed as added protection during combat. Specifically designed to directly counter the space superiority fighters in use by the Rebellion, the shields improves on those used in the ",{"tag":"a","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Lambda"]},"-Class Shuttle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lambda-Class_Shuttle","referenceId":"reference:09ed6c8fc42f5b4e"},", providing a higher energy output for better protection. In addition to the shields, the Xg-1 also carries a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Hyperdrive"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hyperdrive","referenceId":"reference:6774bf610b6e6f09"}," and a larger array of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Weapon Systems"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Weapon_Systems"}," at the pilot's disposal, making the fighter a vastly superior fighter over the standard ",{"tag":"a","children":["TIE Fighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/TIE_Fighter","referenceId":"reference:726e84ae35ac767c"},". The missile package normally carried by the ",{"tag":"i","children":["Alpha"]},"-Class consists of 16 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Concussion Missiles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Concussion_Missiles","referenceId":"reference:c95ee0f6eb24f16e"},", but it can be exchanged for up to 12 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Proton Torpedoes"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Proton_Torpedoes","referenceId":"reference:89c41c332c03f2dd"},", 8 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Heavy Concussion Missiles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Heavy_Concussion_Missiles"}," or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Shieldbuster Torpedoes"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Shieldbuster_Torpedoes","referenceId":"reference:a040cdc2053302dc"},", or 4 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Heavy Space Mines"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Heavy_Space_Mines"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Like so many others, the ship is not without its flaws, the most notable of which is its flight control computer. The performance of the computer is not the issue; the RCS-6 computer system has performed admirably in the past. The main issue is that the system was developed by Miradyne, a computer production company that went out of business several years before the ",{"tag":"i","children":["Alpha"]},"-Class fighter was designed. Why Cygnus Spaceworks decided to use a computer system from a company that could not provide technical support is a question that has largely remained unanswered to date. But, Cygnus compensated by providing their own technical support for the system.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Critics of the design stated that the gunboat's results in performance testing by Cygnus indicate that the ship is too slow and maneuvers much like other fighters in its class, making it a poor choice for a space superiority fighter. The Empire compared these results to other fighters and found that it is less maneuverable than its counterpart, the ",{"tag":"a","children":["X-Wing Starfighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/X-Wing_Starfighter","referenceId":"reference:3633fb1b1140ece1"},", and slower than even the standard ",{"tag":"a","children":["TIE Fighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/TIE_Fighter","referenceId":"reference:726e84ae35ac767c"},". However, it proved to be highly effective against the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Y-Wing Starfighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Y-Wing_Starfighter","referenceId":"reference:ccc65bc19d93864f"}," and even performed well in groups against smaller ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ships","referenceId":"reference:a08d2e2cd508d403"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["History"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Web Enhancements"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Web_Enhancements"}," (",{"tag":"a","children":["Message to Spacers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Message_to_Spacers"},")"]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["When the Xg-1 was first introduced into the Empire's arsenal, it was the only fighter with ",{"tag":"a","children":["Hyperdrive"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hyperdrive","referenceId":"reference:6774bf610b6e6f09"}," capability. Although it was initially looked upon favorably by naval commanders and squadron leaders, its ability to undertake long-range missions were limited due to the fact that no other fighters could escort the ships anywhere beyond the range of their sublight engines. As a result, the ",{"tag":"i","children":["Alpha"]},"-Class ships were forced to engage in heavy assault runs where they relied on ",{"tag":"a","children":["TIE Fighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/TIE_Fighter","referenceId":"reference:726e84ae35ac767c"}," escorts to protect them against superior ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighters"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighters","referenceId":"reference:e127af2636e147fc"}," like the ",{"tag":"a","children":["X-Wing"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/X-Wing"},". Once their escorts were lost, they found their attention split between fending off Rebel fighters and striving to accomplish their mission.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["As time went on, Imperial strategists devised a plan to use the ",{"tag":"i","children":["Alpha"]},"-Class ships on missions where travel through hyperspace was necessary. The ships would be divided into two groups: one group would attack the intended target with heavy ordnance, while the other group would fly as their escorts. Within a short span of time, Sienar Flight Systems introduced the ",{"tag":"a","children":["TIE Avenger"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/TIE_Avenger?action=edit&redlink=1"}," to the Imperial fleet, which also came equipped with shields and its own ",{"tag":"a","children":["Hyperdrive"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hyperdrive","referenceId":"reference:6774bf610b6e6f09"},". The Avengers would accompany the ",{"tag":"i","children":["Alpha"]},"-Class gunboats as escorts, allowing a greater number of the \"Star Wings\" to concentrate on the primary target, while they kept any defending fighters distracted.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Several years later, the Empire elected to phase the Xg-1 out of service, since plans to deploy the newly-developed ",{"tag":"a","children":["TIE Defender"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/TIE_Defender","referenceId":"reference:577e3c60924dbda0"}," throughout the fleet to replace it were already in place. However, Admiral Zaarin's move against the production facilities for the ",{"tag":"a","children":["TIE Avenger"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/TIE_Avenger?action=edit&redlink=1"}," and ",{"tag":"a","children":["TIE Defender"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/TIE_Defender","referenceId":"reference:577e3c60924dbda0"}," forced the ",{"tag":"i","children":["Alpha"]},"-Class out of retirement to stop the incursion. Upgraded with current technology, the gunboat piloted by the Imperial pilot named ",{"tag":"a","children":["Maarek Stele"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Maarek_Stele?action=edit&redlink=1"}," defeated both ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Rneekii Pirates"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Rneekii_Pirates?action=edit&redlink=1"}," and Admiral Zaarin's ",{"tag":"a","children":["TIE Defenders"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/TIE_Defenders?action=edit&redlink=1"},", proving that the ship was still fully capable of serving the Empire.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Xg-1 Star Wings in the Galaxy"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Web Enhancements"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Web_Enhancements"}," (",{"tag":"a","children":["Message to Spacers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Message_to_Spacers"},")"]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The ",{"tag":"i","children":["Alpha"]},"-Class Gunboat's deployment throughout the Empire makes it highly likely that it will be encountered at some point in one's travels. Each ",{"tag":"a","children":["Star Destroyer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Star_Destroyer"}," in the fleet carries five Xg-1 vessels as part of its support ship contingent, although the ship does not necessarily need the support of a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Star Destroyer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Star_Destroyer"}," to fulfill its duties like ",{"tag":"a","children":["TIE Fighters"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/TIE_Fighters"}," do.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Typical missions that call for the use of the ",{"tag":"i","children":["Alpha"]},"-Class are those where ",{"tag":"a","children":["TIE Fighters"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/TIE_Fighters"}," would be incapable of accomplishing successfully. They are sent out for attacks on orbital ",{"tag":"a","children":["Space Stations"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Space_Stations","referenceId":"reference:65763f09c9074f45"},", smaller ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ships","referenceId":"reference:a08d2e2cd508d403"},", or groups of ships as well as long-range scouting. The ",{"tag":"a","children":["Ion Cannons"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ion_Cannons"}," also allow the \"Star Wings\" to be used for situations where Starships need to be taken intact, such as customs assignments.\n"]},"\n","\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Default (Skilled)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Alpha"]},"-Class Xg-1 Star Wing Statistics (CL 10)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Gargantuan ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighter"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +5; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +6\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 16 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 12), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},": 26; +7 Armor, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicular Combat"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicular_Combat","referenceId":"reference:31246426131b3457"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Hit Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hit_Points","referenceId":"reference:58e8ee2c9538d027"},": 130; ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Reduction"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage_Reduction"},": 10; ",{"tag":"a","children":["Shield Rating"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Shield_Rating"},": 30; ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Threshold"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage_Threshold"},": 46\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Offense"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Speed:"]}," Fly 16 Squares (",{"tag":"a",